{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444726-weird-idea-for-accelerating-combat","id":1444726,"title":"Weird idea for accelerating combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-19T16:14:51-07:00","id":1444726,"title":"Weird idea for accelerating combat","content":"I've started to get kind of frustrated with Ex3 combat, and the all-or-nothing nature of decisive attacks. Trading withering attacks back and forth can feel sort of pointless, like you're not actually seeing any progress in the battle. You don't even get the D&amp;D-style sense of wearing someone down. I like the drama of the occasionally big flashy decisive attack, but I find myself wanting more of a simplistic workhorse to go alongside it. A way to make withering attacks just that little bit more lethal and reliably threatening. More like how battle groups work, basically.<br /> <br /> It's at this point that I got a crazy idea.<br /> <br /> What if <i>everyone </i>interacts with withering damage like battle groups do? What if it's a universal rule that withering damage, when applied to a target in crash, becomes lethal? What does that do to the game? How much gets totally messed up, or becomes unexpectedly nasty or worthless? My gut says that since there are more ways of boosting soak than withering damage that nothing should break too badly, but trusting my gut does not always get me very far in this system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>More detailed rules for the sake of argument:</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>The rules of initiative crash change. Your ini can't drop below zero, and you don't gain a +5 initiative bonus for crashing a foe. Instead, any remaining initiative damage rolls over to the health track.<ul><li>ie, if I deal 5 withering damage to a foe with 3 initiative, they get dropped to zero ini and take 2 levels of lethal damage. If my buddy hits them for 6 withering damage before they can recover at all, they take a full 6 levels of lethal.</li> </ul></li> <li>If you hit a foe, you gain initiative equal to the post-soak withering damage inflicted (min 1), regardless of whether or not the target is crashed.</li> <li>To give decisive attacks a slight edge, we give them double 10s on damage rolls across the board-- that should roughly parallel the &quot;+1 damage/4 dice rolled&quot; bonus you get for making a decisive attack on a battle group.</li> <li>Because I'd expect this to lead to more lethal damage flying around, everyone gets bonus health levels equal to their Stamina, starting at -4 and working your way down to -0.<ul><li>ie, if I have 3 Stamina, I'd get an extra -4, -2, and -1. If I bump that up to 5, I'll gain a pair of -0 health levels as well.</li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T16:30:11-07:00","id":1444727,"title":"","content":"Withering damage is bloated on purpose. Making people take damage in crash would be akin to playing rocket tag ala Ex2 all over again. There are ways to boost soak, but you can get absolutely shredded by withering damage either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T16:37:59-07:00","id":1444729,"title":"","content":"I would make the health damage type based on the weapon rather than automatically lethal. Lethal makes sense with BGs because it's a mass of attacks where even blunt force trauma stacks up to more serious wounds.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I think the Perilous Keyword and similar limitations would need some reevaluations because getting Crashed can very severely hamper your defenses already.<br /> <br /> I'm also concerned Decisive attacks would get sidelined. Why bother with one and resetting your Initiative to the point where a lucky hit can Crash you, when you can just keep wailing away with Withering attacks to the same end result?<br /> <br /> I think you could solve a lot of potential issues by having the health damage capped to something like the Overwhelming rating of the attack (potentially making room for heavy weapons to have a better niche in the game). Trying to wither someone to death would be slow, making decisive attacks valuable to end fights faster, but you'd be making noticeable progress as your idea intends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T01:18:49-07:00","id":1444799,"title":"","content":"As other people said, I think withering are designed to not impact Health directly and would not scale properly without adjustment.<br /> <br /> My other idea would eventually be to consider something along the lines of &quot;Every withering attack you take from a major character deals 1 unsoakable bashing damage&quot;, with some limitations : <br /> - No more than 1 per character and per round (to avoid spam)<br /> - Would need tuning for groups of 4-5 characters <br /> <br /> Could maybe be adjusted for &quot;The first Withering you take in a round from a Major character deals 1 unshakable bashing damage&quot;<br /> <br /> This way I think it answers to your &quot;A way to make withering attacks just that little bit more lethal and reliably threatening.&quot; question<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T07:48:37-07:00","id":1444823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1444726-weird-idea-for-accelerating-combat#post1444726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've started to get kind of frustrated with Ex3 combat, and the all-or-nothing nature of decisive attacks. Trading withering attacks back and forth can feel sort of pointless, like you're not actually seeing any progress in the battle. You don't even get the D&amp;D-style sense of wearing someone down. I like the drama of the occasionally big flashy decisive attack, but I find myself wanting more of a simplistic workhorse to go alongside it. A way to make withering attacks just that little bit more lethal and reliably threatening. More like how battle groups work, basically.<br /> <br /> It's at this point that I got a crazy idea.<br /> <br /> What if <i>everyone </i>interacts with withering damage like battle groups do? What if it's a universal rule that withering damage, when applied to a target in crash, becomes lethal? What does that do to the game? How much gets totally messed up, or becomes unexpectedly nasty or worthless? My gut says that since there are more ways of boosting soak than withering damage that nothing should break too badly, but trusting my gut does not always get me very far in this system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>More detailed rules for the sake of argument:</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>The rules of initiative crash change. Your ini can't drop below zero, and you don't gain a +5 initiative bonus for crashing a foe. Instead, any remaining initiative damage rolls over to the health track.<ul><li>ie, if I deal 5 withering damage to a foe with 3 initiative, they get dropped to zero ini and take 2 levels of lethal damage. If my buddy hits them for 6 withering damage before they can recover at all, they take a full 6 levels of lethal.</li> </ul></li> <li>If you hit a foe, you gain initiative equal to the post-soak withering damage inflicted (min 1), regardless of whether or not the target is crashed.</li> <li>To give decisive attacks a slight edge, we give them double 10s on damage rolls across the board-- that should roughly parallel the &quot;+1 damage/4 dice rolled&quot; bonus you get for making a decisive attack on a battle group.</li> <li>Because I'd expect this to lead to more lethal damage flying around, everyone gets bonus health levels equal to their Stamina, starting at -4 and working your way down to -0.<ul><li>ie, if I have 3 Stamina, I'd get an extra -4, -2, and -1. If I bump that up to 5, I'll gain a pair of -0 health levels as well.</li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel your pain...<br /> <br /> The new Exalted Essence Q&amp;A opened my eyes and I will probably unhook the Withering and Initiative like they did in those rules (while keeping the skills of Ex3).<br /> <br /> What I still like about Ex3 is that I can have the combat rules serve the narrative when I have too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and give options to players to make special moves (or gambits).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8757-pram","name":"Pram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}